<h2 id="ha-ctrl-010-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Check exact start/end instants, touching blocks, overlap rejection and an overnight pair across two days. Verify the linked automation does not receive invented off/on transitions.
2. Test an all-day event, a timed event, a read-only calendar and an unavailable provider. Preserve provider recurrence and exception limits.
3. Check the installation zone, a different viewer zone, spring skipped time and autumn repeated time. Record actual native behaviour rather than assuming it.
4. Pause/resume a timer and restart with restore enabled/disabled in a test setup. Verify missing finish-event recovery is explained; keyboard edit and save/cancel semantics remain usable.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

